Z||000000||gt boy||09-30-2001||09:13 PM||||ok i am trying to take off a rear clip from my 86 fastback...it is all loose but the top.  i have removed the nuts underneath the headliner and still it won't budge...any suggestions??<P>------------------<BR>"it's too bad he had to run out of talent half way through the corner..."||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||09-30-2001||09:32 PM||||I beleve there is a bolt in each B pillar. THe B pillar is where the rear speakers are located.  If I remember the bolt is slightly above the hole opening so you have to look carefully.  Oh and be careful when you stick your socket on an extension through the hole because it is easy to knock the socket off while withdrawing it and the socket will fall off the face of the earth, never to be seen again.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||09-30-2001||09:52 PM||||Don't forget the infamous black goop.  It holds everything down pretty well.  There is a bead at the front/rear roof joint as waterproofing.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
